{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 400}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 106, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a conv adds a new learnable path (e.g. +13 to +23 points in #66, #78, #223), whereas replacing an existing op on edge 3 gives only small changes."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a lossy pooling shortcut for an identity shortcut helps consistently (#23, #74, #201, #263), while replacing a conv on edge 3 with skip removes capacity and hurts (#54, #167, #181, #210)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv on the direct edge with parameter-free pooling loses capacity (#117, #146, #292), whereas pooling replacing none can rescue a disconnected cell (#1, #400)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest conv on the first edge with pooling degrades every path through node 1 (#8, #79, #357), unlike filling an empty edge 0 (#75)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning the conv on node1-to-output into pooling removes learned features feeding the output (#41, #131), a bigger loss than when edge 4 was skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With no direct input-to-output edge, edge 4 may be the only path to the output, so cutting it can collapse accuracy to chance (#18)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, the output depends on node 1, so removing edge 0 can disconnect the cell (#99, #272)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is empty, node 2 can only be reached through edge 1, so giving edge 1 a real op restores or strengthens the main path (#14, #73, #185)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on the node1-to-node2 edge with a 3x3 conv adds substantial capacity in the cell's longest path (#159, #330)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv on a previously empty node2-to-output edge opens a new deep path to the output (#383, #392), worth more than swapping an existing op there."}], "tok": 50589, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["none", "none", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "none"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "